WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.534 --> 00:00:03.070
- I think the
world lacks optimism.

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:04.669
I think, you know,

00:00:04.669 --> 00:00:06.306
everyone's like your energy, 
your energy.

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:09.076
I've come to realize
it's just optimism.

00:00:09.076 --> 00:00:11.445
Just happy, just positive.

00:00:11.445 --> 00:00:13.047
Is what it is.

00:00:13.047 --> 00:00:17.150
Just, like, whatever chemicals
are in my body that just allow

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:19.415
me to see the bright side.

00:00:19.415 --> 00:00:20.621
And I just don't think

00:00:20.621 --> 00:00:22.623
I've realized how 
few people have that.

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:26.760
Very few people have
it as black and white,

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.730
hundred-zero, I just
think everything is good but,

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:32.704
you know, I'm dying to know out

00:00:32.704 --> 00:00:35.395
of 8 billion people like 
what the breakdown is.

00:00:35.395 --> 00:00:38.538
My gut is like 6 billion just
go directly into having more

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:42.910
pessimism and cynicism and
negativity like 51-49 minimally

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:46.079
all the way down to
very scary places.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:49.759
I just don't think
there's a lot of 80% optimism.

00:00:49.759 --> 00:00:52.085
- [DRock] Is that the
way they're raised or...?

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:54.521
- Just environment,
raised, just all that stuff.

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:55.856
It doesn't come
naturally to a lot of people.

00:00:55.856 --> 00:00:59.126
I think that's like, you know,
if I was ever to say I'm lucky

00:00:59.126 --> 00:01:01.094
about something, forget
about the business results,

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:04.730
it's lucky that that
optimism comes naturally to me.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:05.599
I'm just optimistic.

00:01:05.599 --> 00:01:10.337
I just think that so much
works for me because I refuse to

00:01:10.337 --> 00:01:13.448
accept the negative.

00:01:13.448 --> 00:01:17.718
And I don't think, I hate when
people say it's an option

00:01:17.718 --> 00:01:19.346
or it's a choice.

00:01:19.346 --> 00:01:20.347
I agree with you, Susan.

00:01:20.347 --> 00:01:21.815
I don't think it comes
natural to everybody.

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:25.152
I think we are just starting
on the early stages of really

00:01:25.152 --> 00:01:27.521
looking at mental
health, the brain,

00:01:27.521 --> 00:01:32.926
meditation and I do think
that's like saying be beautiful.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:34.494
Doesn't come
natural to everybody.

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:35.629
Some of us, you know, yes.

00:01:35.629 --> 00:01:37.130
I'm just kidding.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:41.297
But you know, I, you know,

00:01:41.297 --> 00:01:43.737
I do think that 
some of some things

00:01:43.737 --> 00:01:48.261
are etched with us early
on and I'm so grateful.

00:01:48.261 --> 00:01:51.545
I sit here in front of the
2.000 of you which in itself is

00:01:51.545 --> 00:01:53.914
ridiculous like I can turn
something on in three minutes

00:01:53.914 --> 00:01:57.717
have 2,000 people care enough
to hear what I have to say.

00:01:57.717 --> 00:02:01.488
I sit here with
ego and humility,

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:06.293
gratitude and focus,
appreciation and sense of

00:02:06.293 --> 00:02:10.697
responsibility all built
around really this optimistic

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:14.908
foundation that is the fuel 
that drives me to my hustle

00:02:14.908 --> 00:02:17.580
and to my execution 
in the marketplace.

